1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,500
The Amazon rainforest is the largest tropical rainforest in the world.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
It spans across nine countries, with the majority located in Brazil.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,500
This incredible ecosystem is home to an estimated ten million species of plants and animals.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
The rainforest plays a vital role in regulating the Earth's climate by absorbing carbon dioxide.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Deforestation remains the greatest threat to this remarkable natural treasure.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Conservation efforts continue to protect the forest for future generations.

